{"type":"message","id":"622721a3","parentId":"da398473","timestamp":"2026-03-08T22:13:56.492Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-03-08 23:13 GMT+1] You are an expert AI systems architect.\n\n**Context:**\n- OpenClaw has neuro-memory-agent (Python, 8 brain mechanisms)\n- Evolution service generates code improvement proposals\n- User wants to wire neuro-memory to evolution\n- Three approaches proposed:\n  1. Current: neuro-memory connected to event-mesh (continuous learning)\n  2. Mistral: 3-tier cache (L1 memory, L2 recent, L3 neuro-memory)\n  3. DeepSeek: Lazy evaluation (only compute when evolution runs)\n\n**Question:** Compare adaptive vs fixed frequency for evolution runs.\n\nWhich is better:\n- Fixed weekly\n- Adaptive (trigger when 20+ failures, min 3 days gap)\n- Hybrid (weekly + early trigger if pattern confidence high)\n\nGive me:\n- Recommendation with confidence %\n- Trade-offs for each\n- Implementation complexity estimate\n- Failure scenarios and how they're handled\n\nBe specific and opinionated."}],"timestamp":1773008036491}}
{"type":"message","id":"ea186a4e","parentId":"622721a3","timestamp":"2026-03-08T22:14:35.344Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a systems architecture question about evolution run frequency strategies. Let me analyze each approach:\n\n**Fixed Weekly:**\n- Predictable, easy to reason about\n- Low complexity\n- But may miss urgent patterns or waste cycles when nothing changed\n\n**Adaptive (20+ failures, min 3 days):**\n- Responds to actual need\n- More efficient resource usage\n- But requires tracking state, can be gamed, harder to debug\n\n**Hybrid (weekly + early trigger if confidence high):**\n- Best of both worlds?\n- Safety net of weekly runs\n- Early response to high-confidence patterns\n- More complex but manageable\n\nLet me be opinionated here. The hybrid approach makes the most sense for a production system, but I need to be specific about thresholds, failure scenarios, and implementation complexity.\n\nKey considerations:\n1. Evolution is expensive (generates proposals, runs tests)\n2. Neuro-memory patterns need sufficient data to be meaningful\n3. False positives waste resources\n4. False negatives let bugs/bad patterns persist\n5. The system should degrade gracefully\n\nI'll structure my response with:\n1. Clear recommendation with confidence\n2. Trade-offs table for each approach\n3. Implementation complexity (lines of code, new components)\n4. Failure scenarios and mitigations\n\nLet me be opinionated: Hybrid is the answer, but with specific parameters.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"# Evolution Run Frequency: Architectural Recommendation\n\n## 🎯 Recommendation: **Hybrid** (Confidence: 87%)\n\n**Hybrid wins because it optimizes for the real constraint: pattern quality, not time.**\n\nWeekly is the safety net. Early triggers are opportunistic. Together they handle both steady-state learning and burst failure patterns.\n\n---\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n| Approach | Pros | Cons | Best For |\n|----------|------|------|----------|\n| **Fixed Weekly** | Predictable, debuggable, low cognitive load, no gaming | Misses urgent patterns, wastes cycles on stale weeks, slow feedback loop | Stable systems with low failure variance |\n| **Adaptive (20+ failures, 3d gap)** | Responsive, efficient resource usage, data-driven | Unpredictable, can be triggered by noise, harder to debug, requires state tracking | High-volume systems with clear failure signals |\n| **Hybrid (weekly + early trigger)** | Safety net + responsiveness, configurable thresholds, degrades to weekly if triggers fail | Most complex, dual codepaths, requires tuning confidence thresholds | **Production systems that need both reliability AND responsiveness** |\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Complexity\n\n```\nFixed:       ~20 lines (cron job)\nAdaptive:    ~150 lines (counter, cooldown, trigger logic, persistence)\nHybrid:      ~200 lines (both above + confidence scorer + early trigger logic)\n```\n\n**Hybrid complexity premium:** ~50 lines over adaptive. Worth it.\n\n### Components Needed (Hybrid)\n\n```\nevolution-scheduler/\n├── scheduler.py           # ~80 lines - core hybrid logic\n├── confidence_scorer.py   # ~40 lines - pattern confidence calculation\n├── state_store.py         # ~30 lines - persist counters, last run, cooldowns\n└── config.yaml            # ~20 lines - thresholds\n```\n\n---\n\n## Failure Scenarios & Handling\n\n### 1. **Noise Storm** (20 transient failures in 1 hour)\n| Approach | Behavior | Fix |\n|----------|----------|-----|\n| Fixed | Ignores (waits for weekly) | ❌ Slow |\n| Adaptive | Triggers early (waste) | ✅ Add \"failures within window\" + deduplication |\n| **Hybrid** | Triggers early but confidence scorer sees low pattern coherence → skips | ✅ **Confidence gate catches it** |\n\n**Hybrid wins:** Confidence scorer rejects low-coherence bursts.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Silent Degradation** (no failures, but code quality slowly rots)\n| Approach | Behavior | Fix |\n|----------|----------|-----|\n| Fixed | Runs weekly anyway | ✅ Catches it |\n| Adaptive | Never triggers | ❌ **Critical failure** |\n| **Hybrid** | Weekly safety net catches it | ✅ **Safety net works** |\n\n**Hybrid wins:** Weekly guarantee prevents silent degradation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Trigger Spam** (evolution keeps triggering, never finishing)\n| Approach | Behavior | Fix |\n|----------|----------|-----|\n| Fixed | N/A | ✅ |\n| Adaptive | Can spam if counter resets poorly | ⚠️ Needs \"in-progress\" lock |\n| **Hybrid** | Same risk | ✅ Add `min_interval_between_runs` + `max_concurrent_runs: 1` |\n\n**Mitigation for all:** Guard with `last_run + min_gap` and `status != running`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Confidence Scorer Fails** (returns garbage, always high/low)\n| Approach | Behavior | Fix |\n|----------|----------|-----|\n| Fixed | N/A | ✅ |\n| Adaptive | N/A | ✅ |\n| **Hybrid** | Early triggers become random or disabled | ✅ **Fallback to weekly-only mode** |\n\n**Hybrid resilience:** If confidence scorer errors 3x in a row, disable early triggers, log alert, continue weekly.\n\n---\n\n### 5. **State Corruption** (counter says 1000 failures, actually 0)\n| Approach | Behavior | Fix |\n|----------|----------|-----|\n| Fixed | N/A | ✅ |\n| Adaptive | Spurious trigger | ⚠️ Validate counter sanity |\n| **Hybrid** | Same, but confidence scorer may catch anomaly | ✅ **Cross-validate with event-mesh data** |\n\n**Best practice:** Don't trust single source. Cross-check counter against event-mesh query.\n\n---\n\n## Specific Hybrid Configuration\n\n```yaml\nevolution:\n  schedule:\n    # Safety net - always runs\n    weekly_cron: \"0 3 * * 0\"  # Sunday 3 AM\n    \n    # Early trigger conditions (ALL must be true)\n    early_trigger:\n      min_failures: 20\n      min_failure_pattern_confidence: 0.75  # neuro-memory score\n      min_days_since_last_run: 3\n      max_days_since_last_run: 7  # cap to prevent drift\n      \n    # Guards\n    max_concurrent_runs: 1\n    cooldown_after_failure_minutes: 60\n```\n\n---\n\n## Why Not Pure Adaptive?\n\nAdaptive fails **silent degradation**. If the system works \"too well\" (few failures), evolution never runs, and you lose:\n- Proactive improvements\n- Drift detection\n- Fresh proposals for non-failure patterns (performance, DX, etc.)\n\n**Evolution isn't just bug-fixing.** It's continuous improvement. Weekly baseline ensures it happens.\n\n---\n\n## Why Not Pure Weekly?\n\nWeekly is fine for stable systems, but:\n- 7-day latency on urgent patterns is unacceptable for active development\n- If 50 failures happen Monday, waiting until Sunday is negligence\n- Neuro-memory patterns lose freshness after 3-4 days\n\n---\n\n## Final Opinion\n\n**Hybrid or you're doing it wrong.**\n\nThe 50 extra lines of complexity buy you:\n- ✅ Guaranteed weekly evolution (safety net)\n- ✅ Responsive early triggers when patterns are real\n- ✅ Confidence gate to reject noise\n- ✅ Graceful degradation to weekly if triggers fail\n- ✅ Debuggability (you always know next run is ≤7 days away)\n\n**Confidence: 87%** (13% reserved for \"your specific context might differ\"—e.g., if you have <5 failures/month, just use weekly and save yourself the complexity)."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zhipu","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":2909,"output":1605,"cacheRead":11264,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15778,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773008036492}}
